# nr-exthost-ooxml-text: the new crate crates/mixdog-ooxml-text (OOXML text extraction: ooxml.text, media.officeText, the legacy-Office refusal).
# Written without compiling (no cargo run in this wave); the first compile is the lead's.

## 1. native/core/Cargo.toml `[workspace] members`, after "crates/mixdog-js":
    "crates/mixdog-ooxml-text",

## 2. native/core/Cargo.toml `[workspace.dependencies]`, after the line `mixdog-js = { path = "crates/mixdog-js" }`:
mixdog-ooxml-text = { path = "crates/mixdog-ooxml-text" }

## 3. Lock and hack
# `cargo update --workspace --offline` (adds the package `mixdog-ooxml-text` to Cargo.lock; every dependency is already locked:
# flate2 1.1.10 with zlib-rs, sha2, mixdog-fsio, mixdog-js, mixdog-workspace-hack; dev: mixdog-testkit, base64, serde_json,
# tempfile) and `cargo hakari generate` (flate2 with "zlib-rs" is already in mixdog-workspace-hack/Cargo.toml; nothing new is
# expected there). The crate declares `flate2 = { workspace = true, features = ["zlib-rs"] }` so a build of this package alone
# words a corrupt stream as zlib does ("invalid block type"), as the hack does for the workspace.

## 4. Dependency edges of later tasks (not applied here)
# mixdog-exthost-worker (nr-exthost-worker-methods wave 1, methods/ooxml.rs) takes `mixdog-ooxml-text = { workspace = true }` and
# calls extract_ooxml_text(&proof, path, &ExtractOptions { max_output_bytes }) for `ooxml.text` without part or container limits,
# and try_extract_ooxml_text_from_buffer(&bytes, filename, &Limits { .. }) with them; media.officeText calls
# mixdog_ooxml_text::media::office_text_for_file(data_base64, filename).

## 5. Fixture set index: native/core/fixtures/MANIFEST.json `sets`, between "openai-facts" and "owner-lock" (alphabetical):
#    {
#      "command": "node benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-ooxml-text.mjs --tree <tree of the Node product>",
#      "fileCount": 1,
#      "manifest": "ooxml-text/MANIFEST.json",
#      "manifestSha256": "5908aff31ca663d057b999aa0e71cb2af36ff2c57f6e93e058e1122a3bcfd8dd",
#      "recorder": "benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-ooxml-text.mjs",
#      "set": "ooxml-text",
#      "totalBytes": 1127878
#    }
# (verify-manifests.mjs recomputes these; re-run `node benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-ooxml-text.mjs --tree C:\Project\mixdog`
# if the recorder's lib files changed, then refresh the row.)

## 6. Nothing else
# No protocol row, no SERVICE_PENDING name and no compose_flip change: the methods ooxml.text and media.officeText are
# registered by the Rust worker task (nr-exthost-worker-methods), which owns that wiring.
